    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nA useful advanced follow-up is “What would you change about Lazy loading when the system grows or an important assumption stops being true?” The expected answer should connect the concept to scale, failure handling, compatibility, or another constraint relevant to Lazy loading.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nThis checks whether you can take a basic concept and reason about what changes when the system becomes less ideal or more constrained.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. Start from the normal behavior: Lazy loading defers loading or initialization until content or functionality is actually needed.\n2. Introduce a harder condition such as higher load, failure, compatibility, or security.\n3. Use this concrete case as the anchor: Load a resource when it is actually needed, such as a lower-priority route or image below the fold, rather than delaying critical content.\n4. Explain how the original trade-off changes: For Lazy loading, the useful benefit has to be weighed against the extra complexity, maintenance, or cost introduced by the approach.\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nI would answer the follow-up by stating the changed constraint first. Then I would explain how I would adapt the design or implementation and what evidence I would use to validate the decision.\n\n**Example :**\nLoad a resource when it is actually needed, such as a lower-priority route or image below the fold, rather than delaying critical content.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nA browser application may use Lazy loading when it needs the behavior described in the question. For example, load a resource when it is actually needed, such as a lower-priority route or image below the fold, rather than delaying critical content. The decision should still be checked against the workload, failure modes, and operational constraints.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Treating Lazy loading as a definition to memorize rather than a behavior to apply.\n- Ignoring the main constraint or failure mode associated with Lazy loading.\n- Using it without checking whether the surrounding system actually needs it.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nA strong advanced answer changes with the constraint. Do not give the same basic definition again when the interviewer is testing senior-level reasoning.",
