    shortDescription: "Frequently asked QA Fresher-internship interview question about Severity.",
    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nWhen Severity misbehaves, start by reproducing the symptom and verifying the assumptions around the feature. Then inspect the inputs, state, dependencies, and evidence most relevant to Severity. Severity describes the technical or user impact of a defect. A severe issue can prevent a critical workflow or compromise data integrity or security.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nTroubleshooting questions reveal whether you can narrow a problem using evidence instead of changing several things at once.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. Reproduce the failure and capture the exact symptom.\n2. Check the part of the system that controls Severity: Severity describes the technical or user impact of a defect. A severe issue can prevent a critical workflow or compromise data integrity or security.\n3. Use the concrete workflow as a comparison point: A production crash that blocks checkout has much higher severity than a small visual alignment issue.\n4. Confirm the fix with a targeted regression check and watch for the trade-off: Severity should reflect impact, not the personal urgency of the reporter.\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nI would reproduce the problem first and collect evidence before changing code. Then I would inspect the component or state most closely tied to the symptom, make one controlled change, and verify the result with a regression test or equivalent check.\n\n**Example :**\nA production crash that blocks checkout has much higher severity than a small visual alignment issue.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nA software test cycle may use Severity when it needs the behavior described in the question. For example, a production crash that blocks checkout has much higher severity than a small visual alignment issue. The decision should still be checked against the workload, failure modes, and operational constraints.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Treating Severity as a definition to memorize rather than a behavior to apply.\n- Ignoring the main constraint or failure mode associated with Severity.\n- Using it without checking whether the surrounding system actually needs it.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nTalk through your investigation order. Interviewers learn more from your evidence-gathering and narrowing strategy than from hearing a long list of possible causes.",
