    sampleAnswer: "**Direct answer :**\nWhen Postman misbehaves, start by reproducing the symptom and verifying the assumptions around the feature. Then inspect the inputs, state, dependencies, and evidence most relevant to Postman. Postman is an API client and collaboration tool commonly used to send requests, inspect responses, organize collections, and run API checks.\n\n**Why this is asked :**\nTroubleshooting questions reveal whether you can narrow a problem using evidence instead of changing several things at once.\n\n**Breaking it down :**\n1. Reproduce the failure and capture the exact symptom.\n2. Check the part of the system that controls Postman: Postman is an API client and collaboration tool commonly used to send requests, inspect responses, organize collections, and run API checks.\n3. Use the concrete workflow as a comparison point: Create a collection for `/orders`, add environment variables for the base URL and token, and use assertions for status and response fields.\n4. Confirm the fix with a targeted regression check and watch for the trade-off: It is useful for exploratory and automated API checks, but it is not a substitute for the complete CI test strategy.\n\n**How to structure your spoken answer :**\nI would reproduce the problem first and collect evidence before changing code. Then I would inspect the component or state most closely tied to the symptom, make one controlled change, and verify the result with a regression test or equivalent check.\n\n**Example :**\nCreate a collection for `/orders`, add environment variables for the base URL and token, and use assertions for status and response fields.\n\n**Real-world use case :**\nAn application test workflow may use Postman when it needs the behavior described in the question. For example, create a collection for `/orders`, add environment variables for the base URL and token, and use assertions for status and response fields. The decision should still be checked against the workload, failure modes, and operational constraints.\n\n**Common mistakes :**\n- Treating Postman as a definition to memorize rather than a behavior to apply.\n- Ignoring the main constraint or failure mode associated with Postman.\n- Using it without checking whether the surrounding system actually needs it.\n\n**Interview tip :**\nTalk through your investigation order. Interviewers learn more from your evidence-gathering and narrowing strategy than from hearing a long list of possible causes.",
